[
    RuntimeEnabled=DomicileControlChannel,
    Exposed=Window
] interface DomicileIdleEvent : Event {
  constructor(DOMString type,
              optional DomicileIdleEventInit eventInitDict = {});

  // Whether anybody is at this desktop: true is a desk nobody has touched for
  // as long as its config says, false is somebody back at it.
  //
  // THE STATE, THOUGH THE COMPOSITOR SENDS IT ON THE EDGE. Over there an edge
  // is what a connector can take -- lighting one is a modeset, and a dark desk
  // restating itself every tick is a modeset a second with nobody in the room.
  // A document has the opposite property: it reloads, and one that has just
  // loaded has missed every edge there ever was. So the boolean crosses, and
  // the compositor sends it again to a page that has only just connected.
  //
  // A PAGE CANNOT WORK THIS OUT FOR ITSELF, and document.visibilityState is
  // the trap that looks like it can: a shell IS the desktop, so its document
  // stays visible while the glass is off -- the connector is turned off
  // underneath the browser, which is told nothing about it. Every idle signal
  // the web platform has reads "somebody is here" on a desk nobody has been at
  // for an hour.
  readonly attribute boolean idle;

  // When the browser process had this message, on `performance.now()`'s clock.
  // See DomicileModifiersEvent.arrival for what this is and what it is not.
  readonly attribute DOMHighResTimeStamp arrival;
};
